{"vodka":{"id":"a040e4f5-c526-4d15-9560-4e38699d4a40","word":"vodka","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"clear distilled alcoholic liquor","tags":["feminine"],"word":"vodca"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"clear distilled alcoholic liquor","tags":["feminine"],"word":"vodka"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Eurydice pointed to the cupboard, and sat down on the low divan with folded hands, and looked at the floor. She was quite white. Elsa made her drink a glass of vodka.","ref":"1932, Maurice Baring, chapter 20, in Friday's Business:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[160,165]],"id":"ff1cbcba-62d7-4d9a-867e-588824bc899f"},{"text":"At Vessel, in Seattle, the bar manager, Jamie Boudreau, starts his cherry bitters by combining separate bourbon- and rye-based infusions with a touch of honey-flavored vodka and the Italian digestif amaro.","ref":"2007 June 27, Rob Willey, “A Bit of History, Reborn in a Glass”, in The New York Times, archived from the original on 10 Jun 2021:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[168,173]],"id":"d9e36166-0cbd-4020-9253-eb8198a92d78"}],"wikidata":["Q374"],"senseid":["en:Q374"],"links":[["distil","distil"],["alcoholic","alcoholic"],["liquor","liquor"],["grain","grain"],["mash","mash"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["A clear distilled alcoholic liquor made from grain mash."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"093d9bdd-8fb1-4bb9-afdb-d33d20791067"},{"examples":[{"text":"You should mutter sullenly into your glass, cursing the serving woman (Witch! Hag! Poison!) or the vodka (Poison! Bitch!), as the one pours you another glass of the other.","ref":"1986, Marc Polonsky, Russell Taylor, USSR, From an Original Idea by Karl Marx, Faber and Faber, →ISBN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[99,104]],"id":"216fa8f4-1a20-480b-8246-e5564ee1b99e"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["A serving of th